<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Guaimar IV of Salerno</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1013–1052</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Guaimar IV was the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-lombards">Lombard</a> Prince of Salerno from 1027 to 1052, under whom the principality reached its greatest extent. He took Capua, Amalfi and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sorrento">Sorrento</a> and in 1042 recognised the Norman leaders <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-iron-arm">William Iron Arm</a> and later Drogo as counts in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/apulia">Apulia</a>, helping establish Norman power in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>. He was murdered at Salerno in 1052 by relatives of his wife.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/guaimar-iv-of-salerno.jpg" alt="Guaimar IV of Salerno" width="320" height="273" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: TheDastanMR · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:South_Italy_AD_1039-1047-es.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
